@*
    StarRating.razor
    Purpose: Read-only star rating display with an optional rating count.

    REQ-UI-048 — rebuilt over TrBlazeUI's <Rating> component. The public parameter
    API (Value, RatingCount) is unchanged because PostCard and SearchResults bind to it.

    Dependencies: TrBlazeUI Rating
    Usage: Used in PostCard, PostView, SearchResults for displaying post ratings
*@

@*
    REQ-NFR-007 / WCAG 4.1.2 — TR-031: even with ReadOnly="true", TrBlazeUI's Rating emits
    non-focusable <span role="radio"> stars carrying an EMPTY aria-checked, which axe reports as
    a critical `aria-required-attr` failure and which screen readers announce as a broken radio
    group. Nothing in the library's public API changes that, so the stars are presented as the
    decoration they actually are (aria-hidden) and the value is exposed as real text instead.
*@
<div class="inline-flex items-center gap-1.5" data-testid="star-rating">
    @* data-a11y-decorative — see App.razor. Read-only stars carry no tab stop today, but the
       marker means a library change cannot quietly put one inside an aria-hidden subtree.
       [REQ-NFR-007] *@
    <span aria-hidden="true" class="inline-flex" data-a11y-decorative>
        <Rating Value="@Value"
                Max="5"
                ReadOnly="true"
                AllowHalf="false"
                Size="RatingSize.Small" />
    </span>
    <span class="sr-only" data-testid="star-rating-text">
        Rated @Value out of 5@(RatingCount > 0 ? $" from {RatingCount} ratings" : string.Empty)
    </span>
    @if (RatingCount > 0)
    {
        <span aria-hidden="true" class="text-xs text-muted-foreground" data-testid="total-rating-value">(@RatingCount)</span>
    }
</div>

@code {
    /// <summary>
    /// The rating value, 0-5 stars filled.
    /// </summary>
    [Parameter]
    public int Value { get; set; } = 0;

    /// <summary>
    /// Optional count of ratings to display in parentheses. Hidden when zero.
    /// </summary>
    [Parameter]
    public int RatingCount { get; set; } = 0;
}
